Package: LARItools
Title: Cohort-Level Transcriptomic Classification of a Lactylation-Program-Associated Tumor State
Version: 1.2.1
Authors@R:
    person("Zhihao", "Bo", , "bozhihao@tmu.edu.cn", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-6298-1953"))
Description: Provides cohort-level transcriptomic scoring and classification of a
    lactylation-program-associated stromal-immune tumor state. The primary model is
    a locked 10-gene mRNA random-forest classifier that returns the predicted
    probability of the CS2-associated class and applies a fixed discovery-cohort
    threshold to assign predicted CS1-like or CS2-like labels. Expression values are
    centered within the submitted cohort and scaled by discovery-training standard
    deviations, so the score is cohort-relative rather than single-sample
    independent. The package also provides LacCore signature scoring by
    single-sample gene set enrichment analysis and an optional interface to the
    Python 'tidepy' package for exploratory TIDE analysis. Neither the LARI score nor
    the LacCore score is a direct biochemical measurement of histone lactylation.
